aim in the center, controlling key squares\n- It opens up development for both my light-squared bishop (f1) and queen (d1)\n- It's the most direct and principled first move, fighting for central control from move one\n- It leads to sharp, tactical games which give White good winning chances\n- It's been the choice of world champions throughout history and is statistically one of the strongest opening moves\n\nAnswer: P: e2-e4"}
