ing e4 and preparing to recapture if Black takes on e4. Solid but slightly passive.\n\n5. **P: e4-e5** - Push forward aggressively, gaining space. However, this allows Black's d-pawn to remain strong and doesn't address the central tension.\n\nReason:\n**P: d2-d4** is the strongest move here. It supports my e4 pawn and establishes a classical pawn center. After Black captures d5xe4, I can recapture and maintain central presence. This move follows opening principles: control the center with pawns first, then develop pieces. It's more forcing than knight development and creates immediate central tension that I'm well-positioned to handle.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4"}
