ck's camp) and preparing to castle kingside.\n\n5. **B: c1-g5** - Develops the light-squared bishop actively, but my f1 bishop and king-side development seem more urgent.\n\nReason: I choose **N: f3-e5** because:\n- It places the knight on the best central square\n- The e5 knight attacks f7, a critical weakness near Black's uncastled king\n- It controls important squares (d7, c6, g6, g4)\n- From e5, the knight can quickly relocate to support various plans\n- It maintains pressure while keeping my position flexible\n- Black's pieces are underdeveloped, so active piece play is favorable\n\nAnswer: N: f3-e5"}
