ortunity.\n\nReason:\nB: c7-b6 delivers check to the Black king on b7. This is forcing - the king must respond immediately. After the king moves (likely to a8, a7, c8, or c6), I maintain the initiative and can continue attacking. Giving check when the opponent's king is exposed is almost always worth considering, as it restricts their options and maintains pressure. This move also keeps my bishop active and well-placed.\n\nAnswer: B: c7-b6"}
