he exchange (rook for bishop). This is a clear material advantage of approximately 2 points (rook = 5, bishop = 3). In chess, winning material, especially a whole rook, is typically a decisive advantage. After Bxd8, even if Black recaptures, I'll be up the exchange and should be able to convert this material advantage into a win with proper technique.\n\nAnswer: B: b6-d8"}
