ng Black to respond immediately. After the king moves (likely Ka8, Kb8, or Ka6), I maintain my active bishop and can continue applying pressure. Check moves are forcing and often lead to tactical advantages. This move also keeps Black on the defensive and prevents them from consolidating or launching their own attack with the knight on g4.\n\nAnswer: B: b6-c7"}
