tively in the position\n\nReason: Moving the king to e2 advances it toward safety and activity. Staying on the back rank with d1 keeps the king more passive and potentially vulnerable to back rank threats. In a difficult position, activating the king and creating mobility is crucial.\n\nAnswer: K: e1-e2"}
