ition with limited escape squares. A check with Qd8-d7 forces the king to move (likely Ka8, Ka6, Kb8, or Kc6), and I can continue applying pressure.\n\nReason: **Q: d8-d7** delivers check to the Black king on b7, forcing an immediate response. This maintains initiative and keeps my queen actively placed in the center of Black's position. After the king moves, I'll have excellent follow-up opportunities to continue the attack, potentially coordinating with my bishop on c7. This is superior to capturing the rook on h8, which would leave my queen out of play in the corner.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-d7"}
