e Black king on c6. This forces Black to respond to the check immediately, giving me the initiative. After the king moves, I can continue with aggressive queen maneuvers. Checks are often strong moves as they limit the opponent's options and maintain the initiative.\n\nReason: Delivering check with B: c7-d6 forces Black's king to move (likely to b5, b7, c5, or d7), giving me tempo to continue my attack. This is a forcing move that maintains pressure and prevents Black from executing their own plans. The bishop also becomes well-placed on d6, controlling key central squares.\n\nAnswer: B: c7-d6"}
