o prevent Black from consolidating. Giving check forces Black to respond to the king's safety first.\n\nReason: **B: d6-c7** is the strongest move because it gives check to Black's exposed king on e6. This forcing move disrupts Black's plans (including the dangerous f2 pawn advancement) and gains tempo. After the king moves, I can reassess and potentially improve my position while keeping Black on the defensive. The check is more forcing than d6-e7 because from c7, the bishop also controls important central squares.\n\nAnswer: B: d6-c7"}
