er, **K: f3-g3** also looks strong as it attacks the knight and improves king position.\n\nReason: I choose **R: e1-e5** because it:\n- Immediately attacks the e5 pawn\n- Centralizes my rook on an active square\n- Creates tactical threats along the 5th rank\n- Puts pressure on Black's position\n- Forces Black to deal with the threat to the e5 pawn\n- Coordinates well with my other rook on f2\n\nThis move maximizes activity and creates immediate problems for Black to solve.\n\nAnswer: R: e1-e5"}
