ongest move because:\n- It centralizes my bishop on an excellent square\n- Controls key squares d6 and f6, restricting Black's king\n- Maintains flexibility for my pieces\n- The bishop on e5 is well-placed to support future pawn advances or coordinate with my rook\n- It's a principled improving move in the endgame\n\nAnswer: B: f4-e5"}
